	"comments": [
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " The expand-first hug renders the callback's opening brace on the callee's line, so",
			"start": 20,
			"end": 105
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " that head line is what print width measures. At 100 it holds and the hug stands in",
			"start": 107,
			"end": 192
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " all three argument printers.",
			"start": 194,
			"end": 225
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " At 101 the hug no longer fits and a parameterless callback has nothing of its own",
			"start": 528,
			"end": 612
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " to break, so every argument goes to its own line.",
			"start": 614,
			"end": 666
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " A callback whose parameter list CAN break is measured the same way — at 100 the",
			"start": 993,
			"end": 1075
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " head line holds and nothing breaks.",
			"start": 1077,
			"end": 1115
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " ...and at 101 the callback's parameters open while the tail stays inline past its",
			"start": 1418,
			"end": 1502
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " body, rather than every argument breaking out.",
			"start": 1504,
			"end": 1553
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " A callback that DOES break internally is measured on the head line the hug renders",
			"start": 1880,
			"end": 1965
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " it on. At 100 that line holds.",
			"start": 1967,
			"end": 2000
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " At 101 it no longer holds, and the hug gives way to one argument per line even",
			"start": 2359,
			"end": 2440
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " though the callback itself has plenty to break.",
			"start": 2442,
			"end": 2492
		}
	],
